<title>UK: UK's Prism orders new trains for LTS Rail.</title>
<headline>UK's Prism orders new trains for LTS Rail.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British railway operator Prism Rail Plc said on Tuesday it had ordered 44 new trains at lease costs of 17 million stg per annum from Porterbrook Leasing Company Ltd and Adtranz ABB Daimler-Benz Transportation Ltd.</p>
<p>Prism said the trains would be supplied by November 1999 to its subsidiary LTS Rail Ltd, which operates a commuter line between Southend and London.</p>
<p>Prism said the leasing package included maintenance. The new fleet of trains will run for the final 12 years of LTS Rail's 15-year franchise which was awarded in May last year.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
